      "root_cause_candidate": "In the NFSD subsystem, the function `nfsd4_add_rdaccess_to_wrdeleg` unconditionally incremented the `nfs4_file` access count via `__nfs4_file_get_access` even when `fp->fi_fds[O_RDONLY]` was already populated by another thread, causing a reference leak that prevented `nfsd_file` objects from being freed during server shutdown.",
      "evidence_points": "The patch removes the unconditional call to `__nfs4_file_get_access(fp, NFS4_SHARE_ACCESS_READ)` located before the `if (!fp->fi_fds[O_RDONLY])` check and moves it inside the conditional block, ensuring the access count is only incremented when the read file descriptor is newly assigned."
